  "question": {
    "text": "If the lines joining the focii of the ellipse \\(\\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1\\) where \\(a > b\\), and an extremity of its minor axis is inclined at an angle \\(60^{\\circ}\\), then the eccentricity of the ellipse is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \\(\\frac{b}{a e}=\\tan 60^{\\circ} \\Rightarrow \\frac{b}{a}=e \\sqrt{3}\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\because e^2=1-\\frac{b^2}{a^2}=1-3 e^2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow e=+\\frac{1}{2} \\quad\\left(e \\neq-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\\)"
  }
